# The gates, in the order scripts/gates.sh runs them.
#
# One gate per line: the principle it enforces, a bar, then the command. Blank lines and
# lines beginning with # are ignored, so a gate can be introduced with the reason it
# exists rather than left to be inferred from its filename.
#
# A later feature adds a gate by appending a line here. That is the whole of FR-036's
# second half: nothing in scripts/gates.sh names an individual gate, so adding one never
# means editing the runner and never risks disturbing the gates already registered.
#
# Ordering is deliberate where it matters. The three Constitution III checks run last and
# in their own sequence: conventions first, because a master that breaks them generates a
# type nobody can find; the drift check last, because it is the one that proves the
# committed trees still match their sources.

Constitution I — no wall-clock time|uv run python scripts/check_no_wallclock.py
Constitution II — seeded randomness|uv run python scripts/check_seeded_rng.py
Constitution IV — no literal paths or hosts|uv run python scripts/check_no_literal_paths.py
Constitution V — no tracked-entity vocabulary|uv run python scripts/check_forbidden_vocabulary.py
Constitution III — schema conventions|uv run python scripts/check_schema_conventions.py
Constitution III — no hand-written boundary types|uv run python scripts/check_handwritten_types.py
Constitution III — generated types are current|./scripts/check_types_drift.sh

# The leakage gate is not a source scan and is registered last for that reason: it runs over
# an artefact rather than over the tree, and it can be pointed at any candidate release
# bundle with --bundle and --pair. With no arguments it runs the corpus committed under
# tests/leakage/fixtures/, controls included, so a run that reports nothing has been shown
# to be capable of reporting something.
Constitution X — no leakage in a released artefact|uv run python scripts/check_leakage.py

# FR-043 asks for a CF-conforming export and FR-007 asks for the check to be a build gate
# rather than something someone remembers to run. It packages a fixture run through the
# packager's own code path, so what is checked is what the writer produces today rather than
# a file that was conforming on the day it was committed.
SRD FR-43 — exports conform to the CF version they declare|uv run python scripts/check_cf_conformance.py

# Feature 016 asks that no capture path wait on a fixed delay (FR-019, SC-011). It is a
# constitution rule in spirit rather than in letter — a sleep is a host-clock dependency in
# a different hat — and it is registered here rather than folded into the wall-clock gate
# because it scans two directories rather than the tree, and because the wall-clock gate's
# permitted zones include test paths, which is exactly where a capture path lives.
016-visual-capture FR-19 — no fixed sleep in a capture path|uv run python scripts/check_no_fixed_sleep.py

# A component under services/ is one of the harness's C-numbers, and what makes it a
# component rather than a module is that nothing else is built on top of it. This gate is
# registered because the repository has twice watched a shared shape sit inside a service
# and acquire consumers across a boundary — encode_netcdf in the environment generator,
# read_netcdf in the divergence monitor — before anybody moved it to libs/. It reports both
# halves of a dependency: one declared in a pyproject, and one taken by an import that no
# pyproject records. The couplings that are genuinely right carry an inline reason and are
# listed in the exemption inventory below the findings.
Repository layout — no service depends on another service|uv run python scripts/check_service_dependencies.py

# Constitution IV in the other direction. The rest of the gates read source; this one
# compares two documents that had quietly stopped agreeing — the container directories a
# component names in its own configuration, and the paths the destination's deployment.json
# declares and the Compose file mounts a volume at. Fourteen of fifteen directories were
# under no declared path, which no test could see because an unmounted directory still
# exists inside a container: a component writes it, reads it back, and shares it with
# nothing. It was a ratchet in tests/unit/test_mount_coherence.py until the list reached
# zero; a gate is what it becomes at zero. One line per destination, so a fault at one is
# still reported when the other is clean.
Constitution IV — every named directory is mounted (local)|uv run python deploy/lib/mount_lint.py local
Constitution IV — every named directory is mounted (droplet)|uv run python deploy/lib/mount_lint.py droplet
